    <time>1787767058</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update libad9361-iio to 0.4.0 (first release since 0.3 in 2019) plus a
full spec cleanup.

Upstream now honours GNUInstallDirs, raises the CMake minimum to 3.5.0,
adds a BUILD_TESTS option and a configurable uninstall target name, and
bumps the internal library version from 0.2 to 0.4. The SONAME is
unchanged at libad9361.so.0, so no rebuild of dependent packages is
needed.

Packaging changes:
- License corrected to LGPL-2.1-or-later. LICENSE and the newly added
  COPYING.txt both carry the LGPL-2.1 text, every source file grants
  &quot;version 2.1 of the License, or (at your option) any later version&quot;,
  and the Python bindings declare SPDX-License-Identifier:
  LGPL-2.1-or-later. The previous GPL-3.0-only tag was wrong; Fedora and
  Debian ship the package as LGPL-2.1-or-later as well.
- URL now points at analogdevicesinc/libad9361-iio; only a GitHub rename
  redirect kept the old analogdevicesinc/libad9361 working.
- New libad9361-iio-link-libm.patch: the filter designer calls cos(),
  sqrt(), exp(), pow() and log10() but the library was never linked
  against libm. The spec hid that by emptying CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS,
  which also discarded the distribution hardening link flags. Both are
  back in place now.
- libad9361-iio-lib-dir.patch rebased: upstream computes the library
  directory itself now, only the generated pkg-config file still needs
  fixing.
- New %check section running the two tests that do not need an AD936x
  device attached (2/2 pass).
- texlive-dot2texi and gcc-c++ BuildRequires dropped (the Doxygen
  configuration disables LaTeX and dot output, the project is plain C),
  cmake &gt;= 3.5.0 floor added.
- Group tags dropped, %cmake_build / %ldconfig_scriptlets / symlinking
  %fdupes, explicit file lists.

Built and verified natively on aarch64 against openSUSE_Tumbleweed:
rpmlint reports 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 badness (the previous build had
one no-%check-section warning).</comment>
    <requestid>1373838</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
